      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is an extremely important concern. Allowing someone to change the password or email without 2FA means that person will be effectively be locked out of their own account until *and if* support is able to restore it to the original account holder. Isn't this exactly what 2FA is supposed to prevent against? All the attacker needs is the current password and a previously authenticated session, possibly even weeks old.",
